    "caveats": [
      "Every figure is a measured work count from driving the real getter over a counting presence store; nothing is wall time. rounds is elapsed virtual time under a paused clock with one tick per presence probe, so the probes of one concurrent batch collapse into one round, and one round is one network round trip.",
      "total_probes counts presence probes, speculation included: the chunks required for the lookup. wasted_probes counts probes answered absent (at or past the first free slot); the sequential scan itself needs bracketing misses, so a width's speculation overhead is its excess over the width-one figure.",
      "verified_gets is the certified retrieval of the committed boundary update; presence answers are unverified, per the finder's documented absence caveat.",
      "Stepwise cells whose replay work n^2/(2*width) exceeds linear_budget are null with a reason: the stepwise replay recomputes its frontier from the floor each round, so measuring those cells is quadratic even though the finder's own probe and round counts are linear.",
      "Wire indexing is shared with the reference client (8-byte big-endian index, keccak(topic || index) id, keccak(id || owner) address); the comparison is lookup strategy only."
    ]
  },
